{"agent":"sw-cedefaults","data":{"budget":"","claim":"The 541 knobs across 50 sections render as TOML literals that parse back equal, independent of host and hash seed, in about 16 KB; the 16 default gates add about 8.5 KB when fields equal to GateDef defaults are left out. Parsing once per process and comparing instead of re-coercing costs about 3 ms per process and nothing measurable per later load.","falsifier":"A default with no TOML form (None, tuple, set), a value that differs between PYTHONHASHSEED runs, or a parse above 15 ms.","item":"CE-defaults-file","mechanism":"tomlcfg.value renders plain values; no section default reads the environment, the host or a set; Config._apply costs 3.5 ms because it coerces each knob, so applying only the knobs that differ from the dataclass value skips it while the pin keeps the two equal.","probe":"scratch proto.py in the worktree at a9a8da595: render Config(), tomllib round trip each value, time parse and _apply over 20 runs, repeat under PYTHONHASHSEED 0, 1, 7","probe_output":"knobs 541 sections 50 bytes 16299 none 0; bad 0; parse ms 3.27; apply ms 3.58; load none ms 0.39; sha ca7d5820a1ff5d1b for all three seeds; gates 8465 bytes","question":"Can every Config() default and the default gates be written as one packaged TOML file and read as the lowest layer without changing a value or slowing the hook path materially?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e4dd20d5bafecbe3bd5524d96","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":139254,"schema":1,"subject":"R555dc3c874","ts":"2026-11-05T11:55:55.163806Z"}
