{"agent":"sw-cedefaults","data":{"item":"CE-defaults-file","repro":{"bytes":6710,"mode":"full","ref":"sha256:6900e1d4fe09ce61c92554a777f4c8b423f5173c111a8407b3881e705afec3b8","truncated":false},"severity":"medium","summary":"ddflow wait --lease <path> returned READY ('free of other agents' leases: claim what you need now') the moment UX-output-caps' lease expired, and a plain update --globs then took ddflow/config/_core.py and ddflow/surfaces/declared/setup.py, while its branch held unmerged commits to both and the item was still running. claim promises to never steal an expired lease because a crashed tree often holds finished work; wait and update do not honour that and do not name the unmerged commits.","tags":["ddflow","lease"],"title":"wait and update hand over files an expired lease's worktree still has unmerged"},"id":"e6a63af3d5913adf21ed3f45b","kind":"bug.found","lamport":139601,"schema":1,"subject":"B-expired-lease-glob-handover","ts":"2026-11-05T12:44:04.356385Z"}
