{"agent":"sw-cedefaults","data":{"body":"NOTE 2026-10-18 (RH-contradictions-2026-10-18, contradiction #3): D-written-defaults-are-marked (accepted 2026-10-18) settles this: each value init/adopt/upgrade writes into .ddflow/conf.d carries a managed marker (origin packaged@<version>) and a digest. D-upgrade-config-changes treats an UNEDITED marked value as ddflow's (an upgrade may move it and shows it in the plan); an edited value or one without a marker is the operator's and is never changed without confirmation. Acceptance: init writes the marker; an upgrade moves an unedited marked default; an edited one triggers confirmation.\n\nORIGINAL TEXT (before RH-contradictions-2026-10-18):\nddflow ships ddflow/templates/default.toml holding every default value and the default workflow (gates, pipelines, flow). First stage: GENERATED from the section declarations (`ddflow config defaults --write`) and pinned by a recipe so it can never drift (pin recipe + test); second stage (CE-defaults-source) makes it the source of values. Loader reads it as the lowest layer. `ddflow config defaults` prints it. Measure its load cost. CONFORMANCE: governed by D-config-engine and research R-config-engine-2026-10 (read both first); every knob settable by file, CLI, MCP and prompt (r-everything-configurable); reuse shared engines, no second layering mechanism (B-org-layers is the layer stack); files under 20 KB; upgrade-manifest fragment per knob; no new MCP tool (the tools/list budget has almost no headroom: extend ddflow_configure); the hook path must not get slower: add a measured import/load budget to the acceptance test.\n\nSCOPE NOTE 2026-11-05 (sw-cedefaults): the managed-marker acceptance in the NOTE above is not met here and is left to CE-topic-split and CE-upgrade, which carry the identical NOTE: D-written-defaults-are-marked governs values written into .ddflow/conf.d, and nothing loads conf.d until CE-confd-loader, which depends on this item. [gate.*] tables are generated and pinned but load_gates reads them only from CE-defaults-source. No ddflow_configure parameter yet: DX-configure-defaults-param. Size: 25 KB, over the 20 KB in the CONFORMANCE boilerplate and under D-small-files-30k's 30 KB, which the test pins."},"id":"e21a7e97a0b5076e97bce7bfc","kind":"task.updated","lamport":139609,"schema":1,"subject":"CE-defaults-file","ts":"2026-11-05T12:44:48.743729Z"}
{"agent":"sw-cedefaults","data":{"body":"CE-defaults-file gave the CLI ddflow config defaults; over MCP only the knob rows of ddflow_configure reach the same values. Add a defaults parameter once B-main-red-core-tools-budget is green and surfaces/tools is free: tools/list is over its ratchet. The file is 25 KB, above the 20 KB result ceiling, so it needs the cut-and-say handling of mcp_bound. Writing stays on ddflow_view pins regenerate.","globs":["ddflow/surfaces/tools/_common.py","ddflow/surfaces/declared/setup.py"],"line":"","needs":["CE-defaults-file"],"parent":"P-config-engine","priority":8,"tags":[],"title":"ddflow_configure prints the packaged default.toml"},"id":"ebc4bdd8cc1cf83bc4e315a2f","kind":"task.added","lamport":139610,"schema":1,"subject":"DX-configure-defaults-param","ts":"2026-11-05T12:45:07.807731Z"}
